      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "BRAVE HERITAGE (1) has the most reliable recent form, with consecutive thirds at this track and a return from harder company into a Maiden, giving him the right profile to break through. The 1300m record is the reservation, but his recent ratings and repeated placings read better than most of these. MILK FOAM (8) also comes through the Warrego race, was not beaten far at long odds in SC grade, and gets a more suitable assignment. If she can find a sharper finish she is in the mix. PRINCE OF SPARTA (5) drops out of a Class 2 and is third-up, so the set-up is kinder than his finishing positions suggest, though he still has to convert late work into a placing. MY LUNA (9) has been safely held in BM58 and BM54 company but comes back into a Maiden fourth-up, which gives her a chance to improve enough for the minors. Include. MACAVERTY (2) finished off strongly when beaten 0.8 lengths last time here. One for consideration.",
